{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRpbuyXE6oAsKT3kM4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 6 (Sb 0.36 / Zn 0.64) as the best composition. It had the highest EQE of the three I measured, 0.0064%. That is the best of only 3 out of 30 compositions, so a better one could exist among the 27 I didn't measure. The episode gave 3 EQE measurements and 5 XRD measurements.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 | 0.36 | 0.0064 |\n| 26 | 0.87 | 0.0010 |\n| 16 | 0.66 | about 0 (-0.00008) |\n\n- **Why EQE is tiny everywhere:** all the oxides in this Sb–Zn system should be wide-gap, so they absorb little light at the 2.4 eV used for illumination.\n- **XRD:** I scanned three compositions (4, 16, 26). The two Sb-rich ones (16 and 26) show peaks consistent with the ZnSb₂O₆ structure. Index 4 on the Zn-rich side shows a different phase.\n- **How I chose what to measure:** I measured index 6 without a scan of its own; the index 4 scan was my stand-in for the Zn-rich side. Its result being the best suggests the Zn-rich end, below about 0.4 Sb, is where to look for any further improvement.\n\nI used 3 of the 5 XRD measurements."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":8430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d70d169-0830-4e1a-a2e8-7111eda7a8c6","uuid":"af9c6bb9-07fa-4b48-ae03-f912f478f977","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:06:56.988Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRpbQDiiEzYrsCnFaau"}
